      "source_text": "Good morning, Ziv.\nI thought a lot about it and yes you were indeed clear on your explanation.\nThe way it made sense to me to keep best software practices of \u201cseparation of concerns\u201d, is that we treat this with a complementary application, which we could call the state manager (we can find a better name in the future).\nThe way it works is: * The word frequency tracker would have methods like save state (to a json file), load state (from a json file), and of course all core methods like process text, and the methods for extracting calculated data/frequencies, trending words, new words, etc.\n(everything that is concerned to the word frequency calculation task) * \u2060we\u2019d have this other application called state manager, that would get from the user basically 2 things: the the id of the subject being explored at the moment (what is the content about?\nShips?\nPlanes?\nStock Market?\nWe\u2019ll have an id for it), and the session number of interest (as you mentioned, it\u2019s still hard to conceive all possible filters that make sense) * \u2060every time the user is consuming content and completing sessions, this state manager would call the word frequency tracker (software being developed now) and pass to it save paths for the states, and in the name of the state file we could include those 2 informations I mentioned in the bullet above (an identifier for the subject and the session number) plus the timestamp.\nWith that, we\u2019d be able to generate whichever aggregated or filtered stats we\u2019d want because we\u2019ll basically have state files tagged with valuable metadata.\nFor example, if the user wants to know the progress, we shouldn\u2019t and wouldn\u2019t need to call the tracker..\nwe\u2019d simply leave this to the state manager ..\nit would for example get the latest state file for a specific subject of interest, or do the delta progress from last week to this week, or even aggregate word frequencies among several subjects * \u2060that\u2019s how I see it..\nI think this way we avoid stuffing all kinds of tasks inside the word frequency tracker and making it a confusing piece of software * \u2060I\u2019m not able to include this state manager in the current milestone, but the final delivery would be ready to be integrated with it, and would comply with all requirements defined in the design document, except for the sliding window related ones, which, as I\u2019m explaining right now, I think is a different concern/application.\nLet me know what you think.",
