{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "3a8783f5-cd11-4471-9365-c5b0e60538b1",
    "source_text": [
      "Ella\u2019s approach to learning is based on two core foundational principles.\nFirst, the approach is anchored around learning through content consumption.\nThe content can be in the form of audio and/or video.\nThe content is selected by the learners or generated for the learners.\nThe content is adapted to the learners (or generated) as well as enriched for the learners based on their interests, learning goals, and past experience.\nSecond, the approach is grounded in a new content delivery framework to convey the designated content to the learner.\nThe framework is designed to facilitate flexible, efficient, and highly expressive content delivery.\nIn this method, content is divided to one or more speakers, rotating content delivery between them.\nSpeakers can represent languages (e.g.\nforeign vs native), roles (e.g.\noriginal text vs teacher), narration, and actual speakers (e.g.\ncontent of interview or panel discussion).\nMore specifically, content (of any kind) is first adapted and enriched, and then split to speakers based on semantics or roles, and the content of each speaker is split into phrases based on the use case.\nThe content (in phrases) may undergo further enrichments.\nThe content is delivered by playing it by the speakers alternating turns in a preset order, such that each speaker delivers one corresponding phrase per rotation until all phrases have been presented.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,B2,,"
  },
