      "At dusk, Emberclaw the dragon soared above the silent valley.\nScales shimmering like molten gold, she surveyed the sleeping villages.\nFor centuries, villagers had feared her fiery breath, but tonight she brought gifts: rare moonflowers and gleaming pearls.\nAs Emberclaw landed beside the ancient oak, a timid child approached, offering a single glowing lantern.\nCurious, the dragon dipped her head and breathed a gentle plume of smoke that lit its flame.\nFrom that moment, fear melted into wonder.\nEmberclaw became guardian of the valley, her roar a promise of protection, and each dawn brought songs of gratitude to her name.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "es-ES,A1,,"
