{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "272f580c-40f0-4e49-b2d9-30180979cb1a",
    "source_text": [
      "Central Business District Tolling Program (CBDTP) begins January 5, 2025 Starting on January 5, 2025, E-ZPass customers entering the Central Business District (CBD), popularly referred to as the Congestion Relief Zone (CRZ), will be charged a CRZ toll.\nThe CRZ includes local streets and avenues in Manhattan at or below 60th St, and excludes trips entirely done on the FDR Drive, West Side Highway/Route 9A, and the Hugh L.\nCarey Tunnel connections to West Street.\nTolls charged in the CRZ are based on the type of vehicle used, time of day, payment method, and any applicable crossing credits.\nTo learn more, visit congestionreliefzone.mta.info.\nPlease note that crossing credits, discounts, and exemptions for which you may be eligible will not be received if your vehicle license plate is not listed on your E-ZPass account.\nTo learn more, visit mta.info/discounts.\nEffective January 5, 2025, at 12:01 A.M., new toll rates will go into effect for vehicle classes 1 through 7 and 11 at all Port Authority of New York and New Jersey bridges and tunnels.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,A2,,"
