    "source_text": [
      "A BIG WEEK FOR REPUBLICANS AND THE TRUMP AGENDA ON CAPITOL HILL.\nHERE TO DELVE DEEPER INTO THE POLITICS OF IT ALL IS AMY WALTER OF THE COOK POLITICAL REPORT WITH AMY WALTER, AND TAMARA KEITH OF NPR.\nGREAT TO SEE YOU BOTH.\nAS LISA WAS REPORTING, THE REPUBLICANS BUDGET BILL MOVES TO THE SENATE.\nWE KNOW SOME REPUBLICAN SENATORS HAVE CONCERNS.\nSOME SAY NOT ENOUGH CUTS, SOME ARE CONCERNED ABOUT MEDICAID CUTS.\nI\u2019M SURE YOU SAW IOWA CENTERED JONI ERNST TOOK QUESTIONS ABOUT THOSE CONCERNS.\nPEOPLE SAID THAT PEOPLE WILL DIE.\nSHE SAID, WE ARE ALL GOING TO DIE.\nSHE DOUBLED DOWN ON THAT WITH THE POST OVER THE WEEKEND.\nHERE IS WHAT SHE SHARED.\n>> I MADE AN INCORRECT ASSUMPTION THAT EVERYONE IN THE AUDITORIUM UNDERSTOOD THAT YES, WE ARE ALL GOING TO PERISH FROM THIS EARTH.\nSO, I APOLOGIZE.\nI\u2019M REALLY GLAD I DID NOT HAVE TO BRING UP THE SUBJECT OF THE TOOTH FAIRY AS WELL.\nAMNA: SENATOR ERNST HAS BECOME A POSTER CHILD FOR DEMOCRATS.\nBUT WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE BILL GOES TO SENATOR ERNST AND THE OTHER SENATORS?\n>> I CAN TELL YOU THAT PRESIDENT TRUMP IS WORKING ON THIS RIGHT NOW.\nWE KNOW HE HAD A CALL WITH SENATOR JOSH HAWLEY OF MISSOURI, WHO IS SOMEONE WHO HAS BEEN RAISING CONCERNS ABOUT MEDICAID CUTS BEING POLITICAL POISON.\nHOLLY THEN TWEETED TODAY THAT THERE WILL BE NO CUTS TO MEDICAID BENEFITS.\nTHIS IS VERY MUCH A RHETORICAL BATTLE THAT IS TAKING PLACE WHERE REPUBLICANS AND THE WHITE HOUSE ARE INSISTING THAT MEDICAID WILL NOT BE CUT, IT WILL JUST BE WASTE AND ABUSE.\nTHERE WILL BE A RAGING FIGHT FOR PUBLIC OPINION ABOUT THIS IN THE DAYS AND WEEKS AHEAD.\nBUT THE IDEA OF GETTING JOSH HAWLEY UNDER THE TENT, GETTING THIS SENATOR WHO HAS BEEN OPENLY CRITICAL OF THE HOUSE CUTS, TO NOW BE ON MESSAGE AT LEAST IN THIS ONE TWEET, IS AN INDICATION THAT THE WHITE HOUSE IS REALLY WORKING TO GET AND ESSENTIALLY DEMANDING THAT REPUBLICANS ARE ALL IN LINE, ALL REPUBLICANS VOTE FOR THIS.\nAND THE MESSAGE I GOT FROM WHITE HOUSE OFFICIALS THAT I WAS TALKING TO MOMENTS AGO IS THEY REALLY DO VIEW THE HOUSE BILL AS A NECESSARY FRAMEWORK.\nTHE BONES OF THE HOUSE BILL NEED TO BE WHAT MAKES IT OUT OF THE SENATE.\nBECAUSE THE HOUSE SO NARROWLY PASSED IT.\nSENATORS ARE UNDER A LOT OF PRESSURE FROM THE PRESIDENT.\nAMNA: DOES THAT SAY THAT REPUBLICANS IN THE SENATE WILL NOT MAKE BIG CHANGES?\n>> I THINK WE ARE AT THIS POINT WHERE IT IS TOO BIG TO FAIL.\nAND THERE ISN\u2019T MUCH TWICE NOW FOR SENATORS ON WHAT THEY ARE ABLE TO BE ABLE TO CARVE OUT.\nI THINK WHAT TAM BROUGHT UP WITH SENATOR HOLLY IS A GOOD POINT.\nHERE IS A GREAT OPPORTUNITY FOR YOU AS AN ELECTED MEMBER TO SHOW YOUR CONSTITUENTS THAT YOU REALLY CARE ABOUT A CERTAIN ISSUE, YOU CAN MAKE THE ARGUMENT THAT YOU BROUGHT IT IN FRONT OF THE PRESIDENT.\nTHE PRESIDENT MADE ACCOMMODATIONS TO YOU.\nTHIS IS A VERY GOOD POLITICAL TOOL.\nWHAT WE ARE SEEING WITH THAT RESPONSE FROM SENATOR ERNST IS ALSO AN EXAMPLE OF THE FIGHT THAT IS GOING TO BE HAPPENING, AND IT IS ALREADY HAPPENING, OVER THE MARKETING AROUND THIS BILL.\nREPUBLICANS ARE CONVINCED MANY OF THESE TOWN HALLS, HER RESPONSE WAS IN A TOWN HALL THAT WAS VERY \u2013 IT WAS NOT EXACTLY A FRIENDLY AUDIENCE.\nTHEIR PERSPECTIVE IS THESE ARE JUST LIBERAL ACTIVISTS, THESE ARE NOT REGULAR VOTERS.\nONCE REGULAR VOTERS WE ARE ONLY TALKING ABOUT WASTE AND ABUSE, NOT TALKING ABOUT KICKING NEEDY PEOPLE OVER MEDICAID, WE WILL WIN.\nDEMOCRATS FEEL VERY DIFFERENTLY.\nTHEY SAY THE WHOLE SHOW MEDICAID IS POPULAR.\nWE WILL MAKE THIS THE CENTERPIECE OF OUR CAMPAIGN.\nSO NOW THE FIGHT IS ON TO DEFINE THE BILL.\nINTERNALLY, ON CAPITOL HILL, I THINK THE REALITY IS IT IS GOING TO BE SOMETHING THAT NOT EVERYBODY IS GOING TO LIKE, BUT THEY HAVE TO PASS IT.\n>> ONE OF THE CHALLENGES IS THE CONGRESSIONAL BUDGET OFFICE, WHICH IS THIS INDEPENDENT ARBITER, HAS SAID MILLIONS OF PEOPLE WILL LOSE MEDICAID COVERAGE, AND THIS LEGISLATION WOULD ADD TO THE DEFICIT.\nTHEN YOU HAVE THE HOUSE SPEAKER ARGUING ABOUT WHETHER THE CONGRESSIONAL BUDGET OFFICE IS REALLY DOING \u2013 AMNA:AMNA: WE WILL HAVE TO TALK MORE ABOUT THAT.\nTHE BACKDROP IS THE CNN POLL OVER THE WEEKEND.\nIT SHOWED THE MAJORITY OF AMERICANS, 58%, SAYING THEY FEEL THE GOVERNMENT SHOULD BE DOING MORE TO SOLVE PROBLEMS.\n41% SAYING THE GOVERNMENT IS DOING TOO MUCH.\nTHAT IS A REVERSAL OF A 20 YEAR TREND.\nIS THAT SAYING THAT PEOPLE ARE CONCERNED ABOUT THE TRUMP ADMINISTRATION CHANGES?\nTAMARA: CERTAINLY THOSE CHANGES HAVE GOTTEN A LOT OF FOCUS AND A LOT OF ATTENTION.\nPROBLEMS AT THE NATIONAL PARK SERVICE OR THE PERSON WHO HAS THE KEY TO THE BATHROOM AT YOSEMITE BEING ONE OF THE PEOPLE WHO WAS LET GO.\nTHOSE SORTS OF STORIES ARE BREAKING THROUGH.\nTHE ANALOGY I THINK OF IS THE AFFORDABLE CARE ACT.\nWHICH WAS VERY UNPOPULAR.\nOBAMACARE WAS NOT A POPULAR PROGRAM UNTIL REPUBLICANS IN CONGRESS STARTED TAKING ACTION TO TAKE IT AWAY.\nTHEN SUDDENLY, HAS THIS BATTLE RAGED, PEOPLE LEARNED ABOUT WHAT THE AFFORDABLE CARE ACT DID, DISCOVER THINGS THEY LIKED WERE ACTUALLY PART OF THIS OBAMACARE THAT THEY THOUGHT THEY DISLIKED.\nIT BECAME MUCH MORE POPULAR WHEN THERE WAS A RISK OF A GOING AWAY.\nAMNA: THERE IS ANOTHER PART OF THE POLE I WANT TO PUT TO YOU ABOUT LEADERSHIP.\nTHEY ASKED IF THE PARTY WITH STRONG LEADERS DESCRIBED DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS OR NEITHER, 40% SAID REPUBLICANS.\n16% SAID DEMOCRATS.\n43% SAID NEITHER.\nYOU WROTE THAT DEMOCRATS ARE STUCK IN WHAT YOU CALL A CRINGE TRACK.\nAMY: THE FIRST THING TO NOTE ABOUT THE BOWL IS PART OF THE REASON THE DEMOCRATIC NUMBER IS SO LOW IS VERY FEW DEMOCRATS BELIEVE THAT THEIR OWN PARTY HAS LEADERSHIP.\nTHAT IS A BIG IMPORTANT POINT TO MAKE.\nIN TERMS OF THE CRINGE TRAP, THIS CHALLENGE THAT DEMOCRATS ARE HAVING, WE ARE \u2013 AND SPENDING A LOT OF MONEY TO HOW TO FIGURE OUT HOW THEY GET THEIR VOTERS BACK THAT THEY USE THINK ABOUT THEIR.\nCORE CONSTITUENT HOW DID THE PARTY ASSOCIATED WITH YOUTH BECOME SO \u2013 I THINK AT THE END OF THE DAY, WHAT WE HAVE SEEN ARE TWO THINGS.\nYOUNGER VOTERS HAVE BEEN TELLING DEMOCRATS AND PRIMARIES WHOM THEY WOULD LIKE TO BE THEIR NOMINEE.\nTHAT PERSON WAS BERNIE SANDERS IN 2016 AND 2020.\nBOTH TIMES, THE PARTY SAID, SORRY.\nVOTERS IN THE PARTY SAID SORRY, WE ARE PICKING THIS PERSON AND YOU HAVE TO VOTE FOR THEM.\nTHE SECOND PART IS DEMOCRATS HAVE ASSUMED THAT BECAUSE YOUNGER VOTERS ARE THEIRS, THEY HAVE TO TURN THEM OUT, THEY DON\u2019T HAVE TO PERSUADE THEM.\nTHE CRINGE COMES IN THE WAYS IN WHICH THEY ARE TRYING TO FIGURE OUT HOW TO PERSUADE THEM.\nTHEY SEEM TO HAVE LOST ANY ABILITY TO UNDERSTAND HOW THOSE YOUNGER VOTERS IN THIS ERA COMMUNICATE, BOTH ONLINE AND WITH EACH OTHER.\nAMNA: WE JUST SAW CONNECTICUT SENATOR CHRIS MURPHY ANNOUNCED A NEW PAC, THAT HE WILL SPEND $2 MILLION NOT JUST ON FIGHTING MEDICAID CUTS, BUT REGISTERING MORE YOUNG VOTERS.\nCOMES IN THE CONTEXT OF SEEING OTHER POTENTIAL 2028 CONTENDERS.\nWE HAVE SEEN TIM WALZ, WES MOORE, JB PRITZKER, PETE BUTTIGIEG.\nARE WE SEEING COMPLETE \u2013 COMPETING VISIONS FOR THE DEMOCRATIC PARTY?\nTAMARA: I DON\u2019T KNOW THAT THEY ARE SAYING VASTLY DIFFERENT THINGS FROM EACH OTHER.\nI THINK ALL OF THOSE PEOPLE YOU NAMED ARE BROADLY SPEAKING, IN THE ESTABLISHMENT PART OF THE DEMOCRATIC PARTY.\nAND WHAT AMY IS TALKING ABOUT IS THAT MANY DEMOCRATIC VOTERS HAVE BEEN CRYING OUT FOR SOMETHING DIFFERENT FROM THE ESTABLISHMENT.\nWE ARE A LONG WAY OFF.\nON THESE THINGS THEY ARE DOING ARE THE THINGS YOU DO WHEN YOU THINK YOU MIGHT BE PRESIDENT SOMEDAY.\nAMY: AND WHEN YOU GIVE AWAY MONEY, YOU ALSO ARE OFFERING \u2013 THAT THOSE FAVORS COME BACK TO YOU.\nTWO CANDIDATES, TO LOCAL ORGANIZATIONS, TO GRASSROOTS GROUPS, IF YOU DECIDE TO RUN FOR PRESIDENT, YOU GO BACK TO THOSE PEOPLE AND SAY, REMEMBER HOW I HELPED YOU OUT?\nTHEY ARE TRYING TO FILL IN THAT POLE NUMBER.\nWHICH IS WHO, DEMOCRATS, DO YOU THINK WOULD BE A GREAT STAND-IN IN YOUR PARTY AS A LEADER?\nRIGHT NOW, THAT IS A HUGE VACUUM, AND A LOT OF DIFFERENT PEOPLE ARE TRYING TO FILL IT.\nAMNA: A GOOD AMOUNT OF TIME.\n2028.\nBUT WE ARE STILL HAVING THE CONVERSATION.\nAMY WALTER, TAMARA KEITH, GREAT TO SEE.\nTHANK YOU.\n"
    ],
