    {
      "operator": "request content",
      "source_name": "95c4ce63-0467-4c1b-a274-408d67f41055",
      "segment_num": 0,
      "source_text": "Hello and Happy New Year!\nI am very excited about the year ahead and confident 2025 will be a great year for Nicol members, staff and owners!\nWe have so much to look forward to, let me start by outlining a few\u2026..\nJanuary means Tournament of Champions in New York and we are both hosting a couple of early rounds and opening practice courts to the pro\u2019s to use during the entire event.\nLast year you could walk into the club at any time during the event and see several top players practicing, stretching, having treatment or just relaxing and enjoying the space.\nAs Jamal always says, you can hear the difference in the noise of the ball strikes as you step in the door - very cool!\nRight about the same time we will be getting PlaySight (https://playsight.com) installed for all four courts.\nYou\u2019ll be able to record, rewatch and even instantly review points of your matches to help with in game strategy.\nFor coaching it\u2019s an invaluable tool to help players improve their game through clearly (and potentially immediately through the App) showing them both where areas need improving and also reinforcing when the player gets the technique/movement correct.\nFull details will follow in the lead up to the system going active.\nJust before then, (realize I\u2019m going in reverse chronologically!) we will be starting the Club Championship.\nThis year we are starting early and giving players more time to complete their matches at each round.\nWe will be staying in touch to try and get as close to a 100% match completion rate as possible so the event is a great experience for all.\nAs it\u2019s the New Year email, you have a bumper edition!\nI\u2019m passing over to Jess to continue with some updates and thoughts for the year ahead.\nStay well, stay healthy and always go for the win!\n- Peter",
      "result_text": "n/a",
