{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "177125ba-5b80-4fc1-8acc-8265f5f6f0a8",
    "source_text": [
      "In summary (particularly, in the context of language learning): Play content in audio in both foreign and native language (alternating) Learners can consume (and learn) without direct interaction (like podcast) Content matches learner's interests (learner's choice, or Ella suggestion) Content selected by, proposed to, or generated for learner Content adapted to learner's proficiency and learning goals Audio and video content enriched with learning materials 1.4 Differentiation 1.\nPrimary differentiation Immersion: learning experience in _audio_ to immerse in foreign language Background: learning occurs in the background, without explicit interaction with an app/system.\nContent selected by learner, or suggested based on learner's interests Personalization of content to learner's level and learning goals Integration of micro-lessons (or other content) into the content, and not only as additions; (for example: adapt content with specific vocabulary) Content generation based on learner's interests and proficiency/learning goals.\n2.\nTechnical challenges Personalize content to proficiency level, past behavior, and learning goals; Adaptation of the content/text and of the speech/audio.\n(Applies to both the original content and the translation).\nSplit content into phrases (based on proficiency and preferences), and keep translation of phrases (vs split of translation) meaningful and in sync.\nInjection of extra content and/or speech: either integrated into the content or as \"add-ons\".\nAudio preparation to ensure natural speech when the content is split into phrases; Applies both to text-to-speech generation, and to adaptation of the original audio.\nReduce operational cost through on-demand processing of content; caching and reuse, optimized use of AI models.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,B2,,"
  },
