      "source_text": "Book summary: Sapiens.\nA Brief History of Humankind by Yuval Noah Harari \u201cAlright, buckle up.\nWe\u2019re about to speed-run 70,000 years of human history in the next few minutes.\u201d So here\u2019s the deal: Sapiens isn\u2019t just a history book.\nIt\u2019s a mind-bender.\nHarari basically asks: how the hell did a bunch of naked apes go from foraging berries to splitting atoms and building Instagram empires?\nFirst stop: The Cognitive Revolution.\nAround 70,000 years ago, humans started talking \u2014 really talking.\nNot just \u201clook out, tiger!\u201d but stories.\nGossip.\nLegends.\nShared myths.\nHarari says this was our cheat code \u2014 it let us cooperate in big groups and outsmart every other species.\nIncluding other humans.\nHomo sapiens didn\u2019t outmuscle Neanderthals \u2014 we out-teamed them.\nNext, the Agricultural Revolution.\nSounds great, right?\nWrong.\nHarari calls it \u201chistory\u2019s biggest fraud.\u201d We settled down, grew wheat \u2014 but wheat domesticated us.\nOur diet got worse, our workload got harder, and somehow, we started worshipping weather gods.\nThen came the rise of myths and empires.\nHarari argues that much of what holds civilization together \u2014 money, religion, nations \u2014 is based on collective fictions.\nLike\u2026 money only works because we all agree it has value.\nThe U.S.\ndollar is basically a shared hallucination \u2014 but a really powerful one.\nFast forward: The Scientific Revolution.\nThis is when humans admitted: \u201cHey, maybe we don\u2019t know everything.\u201d And that humility sparked a knowledge explosion \u2014 leading to capitalism, industrialism, and smartphones.\nBut here\u2019s the kicker \u2014 we became gods in our own right.\nWe can now engineer genes, hack brains, maybe even design new species.\nFinal question Harari drops like a mic at the end: What do we want to become?\nBecause now that we\u2019ve conquered the world\u2026 are we any happier?\nAnd what happens when intelligence is divorced from consciousness \u2014 when AIs are smarter, but don\u2019t feel?\n\u201cSo yeah, Sapiens isn\u2019t just history \u2014 it\u2019s a wake-up call.\nIt\u2019s a reminder that everything we take for granted\u2026 might just be a story we\u2019re telling ourselves.\u201d",
