    "source_text": [
      "Learning a new language does more than add words to your brain \u2014 it reshapes it.\nNeuroscience shows that bilingual brains are more adaptable, more empathetic, and better at problem-solving.\nWhen you learn a language, you\u2019re not just memorizing \u2014 you\u2019re rewiring how you perceive time, emotion, even identity.\nYou begin to think thoughts that don\u2019t exist in your native tongue.\nEvery phrase becomes a key, unlocking how other people see the world.\nAnd fluency?\nIt\u2019s not just mastering grammar.\nIt\u2019s building neural bridges \u2014 between cultures, between minds, between you and everyone else.\n"
