{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "48133b64-9568-404f-875a-ce87bd09fd0d",
    "source_text": [
      "In the quaint town of Millbrook Falls, where the local diner served quantum-infused coffee that temporarily granted patrons the ability to perceive parallel universes through their peripheral vision, Martha Thornberry discovered she could communicate with houseplants, but only while wearing mismatched socks knitted by left-handed grandmothers.\nHer peculiar gift manifested one Tuesday morning when her ficus tree began humming show tunes from the 1950s, accompanied by a chorus of succulent plants that had mastered four-part harmony despite their lack of conventional vocal cords.\nThe revelation coincided with the town's annual Time-Slip Festival, during which random objects throughout Millbrook Falls would occasionally phase through different historical periods \u2013 resulting in situations like the post office briefly offering chariot delivery services and the hardware store selling artisanal stone tools alongside modern power drills.\nMartha's newfound ability attracted the attention of Dr.\nFitzgerald Quark, a retired quantum botanist who had spent thirty years studying the phenomenon of photosynthetic telepathy while maintaining a side business selling interdimensional maple syrup that tasted like childhood memories.\nTogether, they established the first-ever plant-human translation service, though clients often complained that the vegetables were surprisingly sarcastic and the flowering plants had a tendency to quote obscure German philosophy.\nThe local weather forecast now included updates on the collective mood of the town's shrubbery, while the municipal garden club meetings had evolved into heated debates between human members and a particularly argumentative cluster of petunias about the ethical implications of pruning.\nMartha's garden, meanwhile, had developed its own microeconomy based on the exchange of carbon dioxide futures and rare gossip about the neighboring yard's controversial decision to install artificial turf.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "es-ES,A1,,"
