{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "25fb08a2-16c1-4049-853d-91f5e9cf5c87",
    "source_text": [
      "Dear Ziv, Thank you for your follow-up regarding how we can proceed after the initial grant research project.\nBased on my experience, organizations typically move forward in one of two ways: 1.\nAd Hoc Grant Support Under this model, I will first identify potential grant opportunities that align with your language learning app\u2019s goals.\nAfter reviewing the list together, you can decide which grants to pursue.\nI will provide a fee schedule based on the type of grant, federal, state, and local opportunities all have different pricing structures due to varying levels of complexity.\nThis option allows for flexibility, as services are engaged only when you are ready to move forward with a specific grant application.\n2.\nGrant Management Services (Retainer Model) Alternatively, we can establish an ongoing grant management relationship where I not only write grant proposals but also: Manage and monitor active grants Prepare required reports and ensure compliance Maintain your grants database Handle engagement with funders on your behalf Strategically track upcoming opportunities This approach includes a set number of grants written per month (typically two), in addition to comprehensive management and support to maximize your funding potential.\nPlease let me know which approach you feel best fits your needs, and I can prepare a proposal and fee structure accordingly.\nI\u2019m here to help ensure your funding strategy is both targeted and sustainable.\nI look forward to your thoughts .\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,B1,,"
  },
