,
{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "7d700f1b-048d-4e14-aac5-695049678955",
    "source_text": [
      "Dust swirled through the late afternoon sun as Colt Brennan rode into the small desert town of Sagebrush Gulch.\nHis boots tapped softly against the stirrups, and the creak of leather was the only sound aside from the distant cries of hawks overhead.\nColt was a man of few words, known across the territory for his steady aim and unshakeable calm under pressure.\nHe\u2019d come chasing rumors of a rustling gang preying on local ranchers, leaving empty corrals in their wake.\nFolks in town eyed him warily as he tethered his horse outside the saloon, a place where debts were settled and secrets whispered.\nInside, the air smelled of old whiskey and sweat.\nColt ordered a sarsaparilla and listened as merchants and cowhands shared whispers of stolen cattle moving south under cover of darkness.\nBy sunset, he rode out to the Yang ranch, where a frightened family huddled beside an empty pasture gate.\nColt nodded and set to work, tracking hoofprints into the dusty arroyo.\nWhen the gang\u2019s lookout spotted him, Colt drew his revolver with lightning speed.\nA single shot rang out, and the lookout tumbled, freeing the path for the ranch hands to secure their herd.\nThat night, Colt returned to Sagebrush Gulch, the moonlight glinting off his hat brim.\nWord of his courage spread like wildfire, and for the first time in weeks, the town slept soundly\u2014knowing a lone cowboy had come riding in to restore justice to their quiet corner of the West.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "es-ES,A1,,"
  },
