{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "5dabdc0c-5386-42bb-a5bc-6b4f1adc538a",
    "source_text": [
      "In the highlands of Vareth, where the wind howled like wolves and the stars blinked with purpose, a girl named Lira was born under a comet-streaked sky.\nHer village whispered that she was touched by Elorin \u2014 the ancient sky eagle god who vanished centuries ago after casting his final blessing on the world.\nLira never believed in destiny.\nShe believed in her blade, in the boots her father left her, and in the power of silence.\nBut everything changed the day the feather fell.\nIt was not just any feather \u2014 it glowed faintly, pulsing with warmth, and shimmered with a color no one could name.\nIt landed before her feet as she returned from hunting, the sky above eerily still.\nWhen her fingers brushed it, the wind stopped.\nThe trees leaned toward her.\nAnd in her ears rang a voice \u2014 \u201cYou must fly where I cannot.\u201d That night, the stars realigned.\nOld magic stirred.\nThe kings of the southern plains sent riders, seeking her.\nThe dead in the north woke from their graves, whispering her name.\nGuided by visions and hunted by forces both mortal and myth, Lira set out to the edge of the world \u2014 where the sun never rose and Elorin\u2019s bones were said to lie.\nFor in her hands she carried the last feather of a forgotten god\u2026 and with it, the fate of all sky-bound things.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,B2,,"
