{
  "testcase": {
    "source_name": "7a580229-2ff8-4fa8-b7ca-a797d20ec9c8",
    "source_text": [
      "Alpha Testers Start Here: Your Ella Walkthrough + Professional Tips for Alpha Testers.\nWelcome to Ella, and thank you for joining us in this early testing phase.\nAs an alpha tester, you're not only among the first to try Ella\u2014you\u2019re helping us improve it for future learners.\nYour feedback will shape how Ella grows, and we\u2019re excited to have you along for the journey.\nElla is designed to integrate language learning into your daily life.\nInstead of following lessons or memorizing lists, you\u2019ll learn through real content\u2014like articles or audio transcripts\u2014broken into short, manageable phrases.\nEach phrase is presented with a translation that matches your language level, along with audio to help you develop listening and pronunciation skills.\nAs you begin exploring content, take time to try out the playback tools.\nYou can pause the audio, skip ahead or back, and repeat phrases as needed.\nYou can also adjust the skip interval to fine-tune how you move through the content.\nIf reading comfort is important to you, try changing the text size\u2014either for the language you\u2019re learning, your known language, or both\u2014so the layout suits your preferences.\nOne feature we especially encourage you to try is the save function.\nAs you come across words or phrases that are new, interesting, or worth practicing, you can save them with a tap.\nThese saved items are added to your personal vocabulary list, complete with the original translation and the context they appeared in.\nIt\u2019s a great way to keep track of what you want to revisit\u2014and to build a vocabulary that\u2019s truly relevant to your needs.\nIf you\u2019re learning a language for work, for example, try uploading business-related content\u2014like emails, reports, or industry articles.\nAs you save terms you encounter, you\u2019ll create a customized list of words and phrases that match your field, helping you gain fluency in the language of your profession.\nElla is designed to be flexible.\nThere\u2019s no pressure to complete content in a certain order, and no rigid expectations.\nWe want you to explore freely and see what works for you.\nAnd as you do, we ask that you share your thoughts.\nAfter each content session, you\u2019ll receive a brief feedback form.\nEven small comments help us understand what\u2019s working and where we can improve.\nThanks again for being part of Ella\u2019s early testing group.\nYour experience matters, and we can\u2019t wait to hear what you think.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "it-IT,B1,,"
  },
  "testconf": {},
  "history": [
    {
      "operator": "request content",
      "source_name": "7a580229-2ff8-4fa8-b7ca-a797d20ec9c8",
      "segment_num": 0,
      "source_text": "Alpha Testers Start Here: Your Ella Walkthrough + Professional Tips for Alpha Testers.\nWelcome to Ella, and thank you for joining us in this early testing phase.\nAs an alpha tester, you're not only among the first to try Ella\u2014you\u2019re helping us improve it for future learners.\nYour feedback will shape how Ella grows, and we\u2019re excited to have you along for the journey.\nElla is designed to integrate language learning into your daily life.\nInstead of following lessons or memorizing lists, you\u2019ll learn through real content\u2014like articles or audio transcripts\u2014broken into short, manageable phrases.\nEach phrase is presented with a translation that matches your language level, along with audio to help you develop listening and pronunciation skills.\nAs you begin exploring content, take time to try out the playback tools.\nYou can pause the audio, skip ahead or back, and repeat phrases as needed.\nYou can also adjust the skip interval to fine-tune how you move through the content.\nIf reading comfort is important to you, try changing the text size\u2014either for the language you\u2019re learning, your known language, or both\u2014so the layout suits your preferences.\nOne feature we especially encourage you to try is the save function.\nAs you come across words or phrases that are new, interesting, or worth practicing, you can save them with a tap.\nThese saved items are added to your personal vocabulary list, complete with the original translation and the context they appeared in.\nIt\u2019s a great way to keep track of what you want to revisit\u2014and to build a vocabulary that\u2019s truly relevant to your needs.\nIf you\u2019re learning a language for work, for example, try uploading business-related content\u2014like emails, reports, or industry articles.\nAs you save terms you encounter, you\u2019ll create a customized list of words and phrases that match your field, helping you gain fluency in the language of your profession.\nElla is designed to be flexible.\nThere\u2019s no pressure to complete content in a certain order, and no rigid expectations.\nWe want you to explore freely and see what works for you.\nAnd as you do, we ask that you share your thoughts.\nAfter each content session, you\u2019ll receive a brief feedback form.\nEven small comments help us understand what\u2019s working and where we can improve.\nThanks again for being part of Ella\u2019s early testing group.\nYour experience matters, and we can\u2019t wait to hear what you think.",
