    "source_text": [
      "Anatomy of a Fundable Startup: Building a fundable startup requires more than just a great idea\u2014it\u2019s about proving your worth to investors.\nHere are some key takeaways from Anatomy of a Fundable Startup: 1) Traction First: Investors want to see progress.\nProve that you\u2019ve gained traction, whether through user growth, revenue, or partnerships.\n2) Exceptional Team: Your team\u2019s experience, skills, and chemistry are critical.\nBuild a team that complements each other and brings measurable results to the table.\n3) Product Validation: Create something people truly need.\nYour product should solve a clear problem and have tested, real-world validation from customers.\n4) Social Proof: Leverage strong recommendations and relationships.\nBeing introduced to investors by trusted sources can give you an edge.\n5) Market Opportunity: Target a sizable market with growth potential.\nMake sure your market is large enough to generate significant returns for investors.\n"
    ],
