    "source_text": [
      "Evening sun slowly sank below the prairie horizon, painting the sky in crimson and gold.\nA gentle wind whispered through the tall grasses, carrying the sigh of the endless plains.\nLone cowboy Jake strode cautiously across the dry earth.\nOver years on the trail, he had learned to listen to every desert song and decipher the ancient marks on sunbaked stones.\nA well-worn leather satchel hung from his shoulder, and his hands moved with lightning speed at the slightest sign of danger.\nSuddenly, a distant silhouette appeared: another rider approaching.\nJake\u2019s heart quickened\u2014companions were rare in these parts.\nHe veered off the dusty trail and guided his horse toward the newcomer.\nAs they met, their eyes locked\u2014and recognition flashed.\nIt was Marshal Connor, an old comrade with whom Jake had once guarded a small frontier town against ruthless outlaws.\nMemories flickered in their gaze, but a familiar spark burned bright in both men.\nConnor tipped his hat nervously and extended an invitation: \u201cJoin me in defending a rural community threatened by a violent gang.\u201d Jake hesitated only a moment.\nWith a swift nod, he swung into the saddle beside his friend.\nDust kicked up beneath their hooves, shimmering in the dawn light.\nEach knew the stakes: innocent families awaited their arrival.\nThough danger lay ahead, neither hesitated.\nTheir silhouettes against the rising sun became a beacon of hope\u2014a promise that their courage would echo through the wilds of the West for generations to come.\n"
    ],
    "source_config": "en-US,C2,,",
    "target_config": "es-ES,A1,,"
  },
